## Code-to-doc traceability

### STUN URI validation (both forms, DNS hostnames, no I/O)
Source: mtypes/http_control.go:637-698
- ValidateSTUNURI accepts "stun:host:port" and "stun://host:port" (line 641-654: Cut on ":", check scheme "stun"/"stuns", strip optional "//")
- Host validated as IP literal OR valid DNS hostname (line 662: net.ParseIP || validSTUNHostname)
- validSTUNHostname (line 680-698) performs NO DNS I/O, only syntactic label checks
- DNS resolution happens ONLY at runtime in SuperSTUNManager.resolveAddresses (device/super_stun.go:120-150)
- Generic endpoint parsing (conn/conn.go:172-200) remains IP-literal-only (line 185: net.ParseIP(host)==nil → error)
- STUN refresh is one-shot at register time
- STUNRefreshIntervalSeconds is in SuperConfigV2 (mtypes/http_control.go:507) and validated (> 0, line 545) but no runtime code reads it — refreshSTUN is called once at register time only (device/super_http_runtime.go:75). The field is reserved/inert.

Doc claim: "Both stun:host:port and stun://host:port URI forms are accepted. Hosts may be IP literals or syntactically valid DNS hostnames. Validation performs no DNS I/O..."

### SSE with polling fallback (fallback-only, not always-on)
Source: device/super_http_client.go:362-469 (Sync method)
- SSE established first (startStream at line 413)
- Polling starts ONLY after stream error (line 458: startPolling())
- Polling cancelled on stream reconnect (line 432: stopPolling())
- Super event hub close terminates SSE: super_control_http.go:231-234 handleEvents selects on r.Context().Done() AND renderer.Subscriber().Done()

Doc claim: "Polling is fallback-only: ControlHTTPClient.Sync establishes SSE first, starts timed snapshot polling only after a stream connection or parse failure, and cancels polling as soon as a stream is healthy again."

### Edge config legacy rejection (LegacySuper + DynamicRoute.SuperNode)
Source: mtypes/http_control.go:609-630 (EdgeConfigV2.UnmarshalYAML)
- Rejects "LegacySuper" key presence (line 615-617)
- Rejects "DynamicRoute.SuperNode" key presence (line 618-621)
- Includes UseSuperNode: false (key presence check, not value)

Doc claim: "A v1 Edge config containing a LegacySuper key or a DynamicRoute.SuperNode key (including UseSuperNode: false) is rejected with a typed legacy_udp_field error."

### Super config legacy rejection (7 fields)
Source: main_super.go:612-626 (legacyUDPFieldPresent)
- Pre-scans for: PrivKeyV4, PrivKeyV6, ListenPort, FwMark, API_Prefix, ListenPort_EdgeAPI, ListenPort_ManageAPI
- Top-level key match only (line 620-621: ^name: or \nname:)
